## Goal
Drive the DEV-35 "usage statistics" branch (showing whether agents read gitreason notes) through QA and repeated cross-review rounds. The slice also covers fixes for review findings. The commit message itself mentions QA tests for origin lookalikes, backup symlink, byte-exact apply and log endpoint edges (DEV-24).

## Problems
- QA found uncommitted edits in the clone and a PASS that covered only the older HEAD, so it had to be re-run on newer commits.
- Two minor QA findings: the lock-busy message named the repository lock instead of the stats log lock, and a note written while the log was locked was never counted.
- The fourth Codex review found that a failed stats-log append could silently drop counters even though the note was written.
- A `-race` run of the usage tests failed once, apparently from the prune loop starving the appender; it could not be reproduced.

## Decision
- Added a dedicated "stats log lock is busy" error, separate from the repository-lock error.
- Count the note in the kept counters when the log line is skipped.
- On a failed log append, keep the counters file, increment only the note count and skip the user-level copy. The note still carries its Usage line. Possible double counting in the dashboard is accepted and documented in the code.
- Made the prune loop in the race test sleep 1 ms per iteration.
- Each fix got its own commit. QA and a fifth Codex review then ran in parallel on the latest HEAD.

